From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:33:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix main-speaker assignment and add Tier 2 LLM escalation for
 flagged audio

- assign_roles() now prefers a clearly louder speaker over a quieter one
  that merely talks longer, so a background conversation outlasting the
  primary speaker in duration no longer gets misassigned as "main" and
  silently suppresses BACKGROUND_CONVERSATION_DETECTED.
- New escalation path: clips Tier 1 flags as overlap/multiple-speaker are
  transcribed (Whisper, translate task, any spoken language), tagged by
  diarized role, optionally pre-filtered against the on-screen question
  (multilingual-e5 similarity), then reviewed by a local vLLM call with a
  schema-constrained JSON response. Result is stored as a non-authoritative
  aiReview note (contract v1.2) attached to the original observations -
  it never replaces them, and only "main"-role speech can ever be read
  back as "reading the question aloud".
- Question context is wired through a NullQuestionContextProvider stub
  for now; no real question/exam-content source exists in the repo yet.
